text:
maria: Heads up — enterprise customer hitting intermittent 504s and long stalls. They see our TS SDK retrying but some attempts never complete (hang until process killed). Happens behind a corporate HTTP proxy. Repro attached below.

alex: Which SDK call surface? streaming or non-streaming?

maria: Non-streaming completions (client.text.generate). They use ts-sdk v1.12.2 on Node 18.17.1. undici 5.11.0 in the stack. Logs show 'socket hang up' then a flurry of retry attempts but no final error sent back to client.

jamie: Can you drop a minimal repro snippet and proxy env used?

maria: Repro (simplified) — note they were reusing the same AbortController for retries: 

```js
// repro.js
import fetch from 'undici'; // or global fetch in newer Node
const url = 'https://api.redwood.inference/v1/generate';
const sharedCtrl = new AbortController(); // <-- BAD: reused across attempts
async function attempt() {
  try {
    const res = await fetch(url, {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify({ prompt: 'hi' }),
      headers: { 'authorization': 'Bearer REDACTED', 'content-type': 'application/json' },
      signal: sharedCtrl.signal,
      // agent/pipeline not shown — default undici behavior
    });
    console.log('status', res.status);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('err', err.name || err, err.message || '');
  }
}
// simulate retry loop that reuses same controller
for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) attempt();
```

Run with corporate proxy set: `HTTP_PROXY=http://10.10.0.2:8080 node repro.js`

ivan: Reusing AbortController across retries will silently cause later attempts to immediately be aborted if controller was signalled, or if controller remains intact it may not correctly reflect connection lifecycle for new sockets. In some undici versions signal state + streamed request body handling had edgecases that caused the request to hang if the socket was reset by proxy and the request body stream wasn't re-created.

support-bot: Quick checklist: Node version, undici version, ts-sdk version, proxy (squid/azure/bluecoat), capture debug logs (DEBUG=undici* or NODE_DEBUG=undici).

jamie: For reproduction please provide:
- exact ts-sdk npm version
- `npm ls undici` output
- Node exact version (`node -v`)
- repro run with `HTTP_PROXY` set to reproduce the proxy path
- full undici debug: `DEBUG=undici* node repro.js`

maria: Customer gave more details: ts-sdk@1.12.2 (peer undici 5.11.0), Node 18.17.1, proxy is corporate Squid (intermittent connection resets), and yes they were reusing an AbortController in their retry wrapper. They also sometimes reuse the same Request object across retries.

ivan: Two clear issues to call out: 1) reusing AbortController or Request across retry attempts is brittle; create fresh controller and fresh body stream each attempt. 2) older undici versions (5.x) had some behavior where a half-closed socket from proxy + keep-alive could lead to the fetch promise not rejecting until a TCP timeout depending on how body streams were used. Upgrading to undici 6+ (or Node 20's native fetch improvements) fixed many of these edgecases for other customers.

alex: Short-term mitigation for customer: change retry wrapper to create new AbortController per try and recreate body (JSON.stringify each attempt) and lower request keep-alive or disable pooling behind proxy. Example fix: 

```js
async function postWithRetries(url, payload, attempts = 3) {
  for (let i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {
    const ac = new AbortController(); // new controller per attempt
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, {
        method: 'POST',
        body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
        signal: ac.signal,
      });
      return res;
    } catch (err) {
      // if transient, continue; otherwise throw
      if (i === attempts - 1) throw err;
      // small randomized backoff before next attempt
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100 * Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random() * 50));
    }
  }
}
```

maria: Customer applied that change and also tested with ts-sdk@1.13.0 (which pulls in undici 6.x) and the hangs dropped dramatically. They still see occasional 504s from the proxy but client's retries now recover rather than hang.

devex: Action items: 
- INF-7223: Add note to docs about "do not reuse AbortController/Request bodies across retries" and provide recommended retry snippet (above).
- INF-7224: Investigate whether SDK should enforce per-attempt AbortController automatically in its retry helper (sandboxed change + perf review).
- INF-7225: Add conservative undici minimum version to release notes (>=6 recommended) and a troubleshooting section for corporate proxies.

jamie: Also add a quick diagnostic snippet for customers to run that captures undici debug logs and shows TCP resets: `DEBUG=undici* node repro.js 2>&1 | tee undici.log` and attach logs to ticket.

maria: Customer confirmed workaround and is unblocked for now. We'll keep ticket open to track SDK patch. :thumbsup:

alex: Nice. tagging engineering to follow up (cc @ivan).

ivan: I'll pick INF-7224, will prototype making retry wrapper create per-attempt controller and ensure stream/body is re-created. If we can, add a test that simulates proxy reset by closing socket early.

maria: thanks team. closing loop once patch lands. :white_check_mark:
